ssociation between Cardiorespiratory Fitness and Impaired Fasting Glucose and Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus in Men</article-title><source>Annals of Internal Medicine</source><year>1999</year><volume>130</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10068380</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="book"><article-title>Obesity: Preventing and managing the global epidemic: report of a WHO consultation</article-title><source>WHO Techical Report Series 894</source><year>2000</year><volume>894</volume><publisher-name>Geneva , World Health Organization</publisher-name><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>253</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wing</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Phelan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term weight loss maintenance</article-title><source>Am J Clin Nutr</source><year>2005</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>222S</fpage><lpage>225S</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16002825</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nafziger</surname><given-names>AN</given-names></name><name><surname>Stenlund</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wall</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Jenkins</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lundberg</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Pearson</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Weinehall</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High obesity incidence in northern Sweden: How will Sweden look by 2009?</article-title><source>Eur J Epidemiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>382</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16763883</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10654-006-900