ly Medicine</source><year>1997</year><volume>Ph.D.</volume><publisher-name>Ume&#x000e5; , Ume&#x000e5; University</publisher-name><fpage>61</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ohgren</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Weinehall</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Stegmayr</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Boman</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallmans</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Wall</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What else adds to hypertension in predicting stroke? An incident case-referent study</article-title><source>J Intern Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>248</volume><fpage>475</fpage><lpage>482</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11155140</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2796.2000.00746.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reinauer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Home</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanagasabapathy</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Heuck</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><source>Laboratory Diagnosis and Monitoring of Diabetes Mellitus</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Geneva, Switzerland , World Health Organization</publisher-name><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>22</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weinehall</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hellsten</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Boman</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallmans</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pr